# This is a template, not a real credentials file -- the actual .htpasswd
# next to this one is gitignored and must be generated locally, never
# committed (see the past incident referenced in
# tests/testthat/validation.yaml about a hardcoded DB password shipped in
# package source -- same mistake, don't repeat it here).
#
# One proxy credential per person, not one shared line. This is
# deliberately a *separate* credential from that person's SigRepo api_key,
# not the same value reused:
#   - api_key is checked per tool call, inside sigrepo-mcp, passed as a
#     plain JSON argument.
#   - the proxy credential gates whether a request reaches sigrepo-mcp at
#     all, checked via HTTP Basic Auth.
# Keeping them separate means a leak of one (e.g. an api_key showing up in
# a tool-call log somewhere) doesn't also compromise the other.
#
# To add someone:
#   mcp/proxy/add_mcp_proxy_user.sh <username>
# Prints their password once -- relay it out-of-band, nothing stores it.
#
# To remove someone:
#   mcp/proxy/remove_mcp_proxy_user.sh <username>
#
# Either way, reload the running proxy for the change to take effect:
#   docker exec sigrepo-mcp-proxy nginx -s reload
#
# Example of what a resulting line looks like (this hash is not a real secret):
# alice:$apr1$abcd1234$examplehashvalueonly1234
